That makes sense, but it could also be argued that if you do X, then you shall always do Y, then perhaps that should be a single function Z, e.g.

```
static void foo(void)
{
    /* Do foo */
}

static void bar(void)
{
    /* Do bar */
}

void foobar(void)
{
    /* foo shall always be called before bar, and bar shall always be called after foo */
    foo();
    bar();
}
```
